  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Black people are not entitled to cultural or historical artifacts",
  "description": "This stereotype implies that Black people are inherently disconnected from or unworthy of owning cultural or historical artifacts, often used to justify the appropriation or exclusion of Black people from heritage and history. It is a form of racialized historical erasure and is rooted in systemic racism.",
